-- Client-side rows for three server-only spells.
--
-- 24395/24396/24397 are the pet-side mechanic-immunity halves of Bestial Wrath.
-- AzerothCore injects them through the server `spell_dbc` override table, and
-- they exist in NO client Spell.dbc -- not ours, and not the pristine 3.3.5a
-- baseline in dbc/base/retail/.  A hunter who knows Bestial Wrath therefore has
-- three spells the client cannot resolve, so GetSpellLink() on them raises
-- "Invalid spell slot".  That aborts LibSpellRange's UpdateBook("pet") scan
-- partway through, leaving every pet spell after that slot unindexed for
-- WeakAuras range checks.
--
-- These were the only three spells (out of 3,464 known across all characters)
-- missing from the client's spell set, so adding them closes the gap entirely.
--
-- Fields mirror the server rows rather than cloning 19574 wholesale.  In
-- particular Attributes keeps 0x80 DO_NOT_DISPLAY -- clone 19574's attributes
-- instead and the pet grows three phantom buff icons.  Cooldown, mana cost,
-- spell visual, family mask and the description/tooltip text are all cleared
-- for the same reason: this row exists to be linkable, not to be seen.
--
-- The server is unaffected: DBCDatabaseLoader applies `spell_dbc` over the file
-- records, so the server-side definitions still win.

